<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Credit Suisse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1856">1856</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Schweizerische Kreditanstalt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Credit Suisse was a Swiss bank founded in Zurich in 1856 by Alfred Escher, originally to finance railway building, and for long one of the country's two largest banks. After a series of losses and scandals, a loss of confidence in March 2023 led the Swiss authorities to arrange its emergency takeover by UBS, ending its existence as an independent bank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/credit-suisse.jpg" alt="Credit Suisse" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Credit_Suisse_-_Paradeplatz_2011-08-01_16-35-48_ShiftN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
